WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.117
Open the intended call in Omni Dispatch, then select
Records.

00:00:04.297 --> 00:00:06.815
This view shows the records linked to this call.

00:00:06.995 --> 00:00:10.835
Choose New Record to start a department form in the
call context.

00:00:11.155 --> 00:00:15.229
Choose the published Dispatch coordination note for
this exercise.

00:00:15.409 --> 00:00:17.756
Your department may offer different forms.

00:00:17.936 --> 00:00:22.480
The form you choose determines which fields,
permissions and review steps apply.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.485
Enter a Summary and Notes.

00:00:24.665 --> 00:00:28.271
This fictional example records a briefing-location
handoff.

00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:35.704
Search and rescue, community outreach and security
dispatch desks can use the same approach for their
department forms.

00:00:35.884 --> 00:00:37.207
Choose Save and send.

00:00:37.527 --> 00:00:40.791
The server opens the saved record and marks it Draft.

00:00:40.971 --> 00:00:44.619
Verify the form and the saved values before going
further.

00:00:44.799 --> 00:00:46.825
A saved draft can still be edited.

00:00:47.145 --> 00:00:52.969
For this exercise, check the attestation after
reviewing the information, then choose Finalize.

00:00:53.149 --> 00:00:58.056
Use the lifecycle steps required by your department
for the form you are completing.

00:00:58.376 --> 00:01:01.768
Check the permanent record number and the Finalized
status.

00:01:01.948 --> 00:01:05.596
Those are the signals that this record completed its
lifecycle.

00:01:05.916 --> 00:01:08.497
Return to the call and open Records again.

00:01:08.677 --> 00:01:12.005
The same number and Finalized status appear in the
list.

00:01:12.185 --> 00:01:16.132
That gives the next dispatcher a reliable way to find
the handoff.
